<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Brasidas</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 422 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/5th-century-bce">5th century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Brasidas was a Spartan general of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peloponnesian-war">Peloponnesian War</a>. In 424 BCE he marched through <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thessaly">Thessaly</a> to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chalcidice">Chalcidice</a>, where he won over Athenian allies and captured Amphipolis. He was killed in 422 BCE defending Amphipolis in the battle where the Athenian leader <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cleon">Cleon</a> also died, and the city honoured him as its founder.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/brasidas.jpg" alt="Brasidas" width="320" height="450" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Walter Crane · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:He_became_a_target_for_every_arrow_(cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>The 700 helots who marched with <b>Brasidas</b> to the Chalcidice in 424 BCE were later freed and known as the Brasidians, and freed helots in general were called neodamodeis, a name taken to mean something like “new members of the people”.</blockquote><a href="/societies/sparta">Social Hierarchy of Ancient Sparta</a></li><li><blockquote>It governed itself through an assembly and magistrates, honoured Hagnon as founder and later the Spartan <b>Brasidas</b>, and grew rich on timber for shipbuilding, precious metals and trade with Thrace and Macedon.</blockquote><a href="/state/amphipolis">Amphipolis</a></li><li><blockquote>With help from the Spartan <b>Brasidas</b> in 424 BCE it secured its independence from Athens.</blockquote><a href="/state/chalcidian-league">Chalcidian League</a></li></ul></section>
<section class="enc-where enc-born"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Born and died</h2><p class="enc-born-p">Born in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sparta">Sparta</a>, in what is now <a href="/countries/greece">Greece</a>. Died in Amphipolis, in what is now <a href="/countries/greece">Greece</a>. <span class="enc-born-src">Places as Wikidata records them.</span></p><figure class="st-locator enc-loc"><a href="/atlas?at=37.07,22.43&amp;year=-432" aria-label="Sparta on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5112 828 900 540" role="img" aria-label="Map: the birthplace of Brasidas"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5562 1098h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5562 1098h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks the birthplace. <a href="/atlas?at=37.07,22.43&amp;year=-432">What was here in 432 BCE? &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></section>
